# NOT CONSULTED BY THE BUILD.
#
# bin/build-release.sh carries its own --exclude list and never reads this file;
# the only reference to .distignore in that script is the flag that keeps this
# file itself out of the zip. So an entry here governs nothing.
#
# Verified 2026-08-08: CHANGELOG.md is listed below and ships in the dist zip
# anyway, in both plugins.
#
# Kept because `wp dist-archive` and similar tooling DO read it, so it is the
# right place to record intent — but the authoritative list for our own releases
# is the --exclude block in bin/build-release.sh. Change both, or neither.
#
# Not wired together deliberately: build-release.sh already carries a guard for a
# 1.2.1 regression where an over-broad exclude stripped a required file, so
# applying this list wholesale is a real risk that wants its own testing pass.

# Files to exclude from plugin distribution.
# Plugin is private (wbcomdesigns) — not destined for wordpress.org, so
# the dist tarball drops anything that's only useful for development /
# CI / QA / planning.
.git
.gitignore
.gitmodules
.distignore
.editorconfig
.eslintrc
.phpcs.xml.dist
.phpunit.result.cache
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json
phpcs.xml
phpstan.neon
phpstan-baseline.neon
phpstan-bootstrap.php
phpstan-stubs
composer.json
composer.lock
phpunit.xml.dist
webpack.config.js
# Anchored to the plugin root with a leading slash. Bare patterns (src, bin,
# tests) are gitignore-style and match at EVERY depth — which silently stripped
# libs/wbcom-credits-sdk/src from the 1.2.1 zip and broke credit features on
# every fresh install. Keep these root-anchored so bundled SDKs under libs/ ship.
/src
/bin
/tests
CLAUDE.md
CHANGELOG.md
/plan
/audit
.contract-audit-baseline.json
